- mesa_wire

' The switch that gives a world its foot at /<self>/io/mesa. The foot itself
' is all in src/foil. When a world starts with this mount, the mount calls
' mesa_wire/start, which registers the foot.
'
' The foot needs nothing from outside the world:
' - the first time, Mesa makes the world's key, in a file only the runtime
'   reads
' - Mesa keeps its files for the world where the foot's record says, or in
'   io/mesa/
' - if the record holds a port, the foot makes its socket on that port
'
' A port and the cards of peers are ordinary records. Any door or hand can
' write them.
+ mesa_mount
  + start
    \ server=nat self=iota arguments=row[str]
    ^ nat
    | mesa_wire/start server self arguments
